RSM execution requires:

1.  r_sigit   ..  atmospheric initial condition at t0
2.  r_sigitdt ..  atmospheric initial condition at t0+dt (same as r_sigit at t=0)
3.  r_sfci    ..  surface initial condition
4.  sigit     ..  global atmospheric state at t0
5.  sigitdt   ..  global atmospheric state at t+nesting_hour   

6.  regional orography  (constant through out forecast)
7.  regional orography variance (constant through out forecast)
8.  co2 vertical profile (constant through out forecast)
9.  ozone production (constant through out forecast)
10.  ozone loss (constant through out forecast)
11.  cloudiness tuning (constant through out forecast)
12.  ozone latitude-height profile (constant through out forecast)

13.  regional land sea mask (constant through out forecast)
14.  grib global high resolution mask (constant through out forecast)
15.  grib glacier points (constant through out forecast)
16.  grib maximum ice extent (constant through out forecast)
17.  grib sea ice cover (daily variable)
18.  grib snow cover (daily variable)
19.  grib sst (daily variable)
20.  grib albedo fractiona(seasonally variable)
21.  grib vegetation fraction (monthly variable)

How the files are generated:

1, and 3 are generated from sigit and sfci of global model using rinpg program at t=0.
4 and 5 are always given as input file that varies with time.

6, 7 are computed by rmtn program at t=0

8, 9, 10, 11, 12 are binary files in libs/con directory.  They are originally ascii files but are converted to binary when 'make' is issued in libs diretory.

13 is computed by rmtn program at t=0

14-21 are grib files in libs/con directory.  They are originally a packed binary grib file but are unpacked when 'make' is issued in libs directory.

tparm data:

SWHR_GBL ..  short wave radiation computation interval for global model (do not change)

LWHR_GBL .. same as above but for long wave radiation.

INCHOUR .. Forecast hour per one exeution of rfcst.x (depend on the wall clock time required to make forecast.  At least 24.  240-720 recommended).

INSTIG .. r_sig file output interval.  1 hour is target.

ENDHOUR .. End of the forecast integration.  For your project, this is 50year*365days*24hour.

DELTAT_REG .. 10-40 secs.  We should try to use as large a value as possible.

NEST_SEC .. Nesting interval.  We have reanalysis every 6 hours, thus this should be 6*3600

SWHR_REG .. short wave radiation computation interval for regional model (1 hour)

LWHR_REG .. long wave radiation computation interval for regional model (1 hour)

STRHR_REG .. start forecast hour (not used and should be set to 0.)

LOCDF_REG ..  Local diffusion option (should be 0.)

BNDRLXREG ..  Switch for boundary relaxation (should be 1.)

INTSFCX .. Grib surface file merging interval (should be greater than or equal to 24.  24 recommended)


Output from r_fcst

R_sig.ft*, r_flx.ft* , r_pgb.ft*, r_sfc.ft*, r_sigit, r_sigitdt, r_sfci

R_pgb.ft* is generated from r_sig.ft* and r_flx.ft* using rpgb program.

r_sigit, r_sigitdt and rsfi files are restart files. 

